public class Cleanup {
    static class Res implements AutoCloseable {
        final String name;
        Res(String name) { this.name = name; System.out.println("open " + name); }
        @Override public void close() { System.out.println("close " + name); }
    }

    static int parse(String line) {
        try (Res file = new Res("file"); Res reader = new Res("reader")) {
            return Integer.parseInt(line);             // may throw.
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(parse("42"));
        try { parse("oops"); }
        catch (NumberFormatException e) { System.out.println("bad input"); }
    }
}
```

Output: open file, open reader, close reader, close file, 42, then the same four lines again before bad input. Cleanup runs on both paths.

